    "title": {
      "en": "Forgotten Dungeon Loot Mailed to Players in WoW: Forever",
      "es": "Botín de mazmorras olvidadas enviado por correo a los jugadores en WoW: Forever"
    },
    "summary": {
      "en": "Forgotten Dungeon Loot Mailed to Players in WoW: Forever...",
      "es": "Botín de mazmorra olvidado enviado por correo a los jugadores en WoW: Forever..."
    },
    "contentHtml": "\n            <div id=\"news-post-6ab19c53ba2a69.05219121\" data-insert-ads=\"article\" data-zaf-dynamic=\"article\" data-units-dynamic=\"article\" data-zaf-slot=\"true\">A feature from Modern World of Warcraft has made its way into WoW Forever. Any loot not picked up by players in a dungeon will be mailed to them now, thanks to the Steamwheelde Lost and Found.<h2 id=\"new-loot-recovery-system-in-wow-forever\" class=\"heading-size-2 heading-bar\"><span data-markup-content-target=\"1\">New Loot Recovery System in WoW Forever</span></h2><div class=\"pad exclude-units\"></div>Players tend to unfortunately forget to pick up a piece of loot, whether Uncommon, Rare, or even Epic in Classic WoW. The consequence of this is that if you realize too late, the NPC with said loot can despawn, offering no opportunity for recovery - you have to hope it drops again in the next run. In World of Warcraft: Forever, the Steamwheedle Lost and Found makes sure players get all their items from instances, even if they didn't realize their bag was full at the time!<br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><a href=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1302388.png\" id=\"1302388\"><img width=\"700\" src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1302388.png\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"content-image border\" alt=\"Steamwheedle Lost and Found WoW Forever\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; border-width: 2px;\"></a></div><br><br>Players can thank Rix Xizzix, owner of the Steamwheedle Lost and Found, for assisting them with their oversights. Players may remember this goblin and his organization from Season of Discovery, as it appears they've made a permanent return in WoW Forever.<br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><a href=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1302387.jpg\" id=\"1302387\"><img width=\"700\" src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1302387.jpg?maxWidth=700\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"content-image border\" alt=\"Steamwheedle Lost and Found WoW Forever\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; border-width: 2px;\"></a><br><i>Note: The letter does not actually self-destruct, but don't take any chances!</i></div></div>\n            \n            <noscript>A feature from Modern World of Warcraft has made its way into WoW Forever. Any loot not picked up by players in a dungeon will be mailed to them now, thanks to the Steamwheelde Lost and Found.<br /><br /><h2 class=\"heading-size-2\">New Loot Recovery System in WoW Forever</h2><br /><br />Players tend to unfortunately forget to pick up a piece of loot, whether Uncommon, Rare, or even Epic in Classic WoW. The consequence of this is that if you realize too late, the NPC with said loot can despawn, offering no opportunity for recovery - you have to hope it drops again in the next run. In World of Warcraft: Forever, the Steamwheedle Lost and Found makes sure players get all their items from instances, even if they didn't realize their bag was full at the time!<br /><br />Players can thank Rix Xizzix, owner of the Steamwheedle Lost and Found, for assisting them with their oversights. Players may remember this goblin and his organization from Season of Discovery, as it appears they've made a permanent return in WoW Forever.<br /><br /><i>Note: The letter does not actually self-destruct, but don't take any chances!</i></noscript>            \n        ",
